## JAKA SDK binaries

`jaka_arm/jaka_sdk/aarch64-linux-gnu/{jkrc.so,libjakaAPI.so}` (jkrc Python
SDK, pyV2.1.7.0, Linux aarch64) are unmodified binaries from the JAKA (节卡)
official SDK download (https://www.jaka.com/download — 资料中心 → 二次开发
→ SDK). JAKA publishes the SDK under the Apache License 2.0: the SDK's
C/C++ headers carry "Copyright (c) JAKA Robotics, Ltd. … Licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0", and JAKA's official SDK repositories
(https://github.com/JAKARobotics) are Apache-2.0 as well. A copy of the
license is at `jaka_arm/jaka_sdk/LICENSE`.

Other platform sets (`x86_64-linux-gnu`, `windows`) are gitignored — download
the SDK for your arch and place both files under
`jaka_arm/jaka_sdk/<platform>/`. The loader in `jaka_arm/jaka_sdk/__init__.py`
picks the platform automatically, and `scripts/build.sh` fails fast with
these instructions when they are missing.
